# Select default (LOCKED)

When creating a select, use the Org EHG Select glass lock in
`src/Products/PinoyBusinessPOS/ExItS.PinoyBusinessPOS.React/src/features/ui-standards/org-enterprise-hybrid-glass/org-ehg-select-glass-global-default.ts`.

The locked command is `ext org-ehg select-glass qa primary stacked md icon-none shape-standard no-shadow`.

Product component: `ExitsOrgEhgSelect` — use this whenever the surface is Org EHG. Do not invent another EHG select recipe.

Full recipe: `.cursor/rules/exits-org-ehg-select-glass.mdc`.

- Tone: primary
- Appearance: stacked (Label above)
- Size: md
- Icon: none
- Shape: standard
- Shadow: off

UI Standards **Select glass** playground seeds this lock. Do not invent a flat Material select or Soft Glass CompactSelect unless the user names Soft Glass primary fields (`exits-soft-glass-primary-fields.mdc`) or another recipe.

## Soft Glass exception

Personal Soft Glass primary field groups still use locked `CompactSelect` (`ext dropdown primary outlined`) under `exits-soft-glass-primary-fields.mdc`. That Soft Glass path is separate from this global select creation lock.

## Type (when using Soft Glass / Form Components CompactSelect)

The lock in `field-typography-global-default.ts` still covers Soft Glass / Form Components select type (13px label, 14px value, open bar). Do not put those type values in the Org EHG select-glass lock file.

Change the Org EHG select creation lock only when the user asks. Update `org-ehg-select-glass-global-default.ts`, `org-ehg-select-glass-global-default.test.ts`, `OrgEhgQaSelectGlassPlayground.tsx`, `exits-org-ehg-select-glass.mdc`, and this rule together.
